    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nI found [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1238) in the current codebase. I suppose this is intended to make the `S` marker (for snippets) visible only when there are actual snippets. However, this can lead to inconsistent behavior for functions:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b427f4be-2485-4890-9b2b-6e0ac25fb066\n\nAfter removing it, typing the two functions have the same behavior:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f48ad107-3ea1-44fa-a747-66e2e2810e61\n\nAlthough it's nice to have a smarter indicator, I believe this issue should be addressed on the server side or client side through `lsp_completion.process_items`.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nThe minimal reproducing configuration:\n\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\n\nrequire('mini.completion').setup()\nvim.o.signcolumn = 'yes'\n\n-- https://pkg.go.dev/golang.org/x/tools/gopls\nvim.lsp.config('gopls', {\n  cmd = { 'gopls' },\n  filetypes = { 'go' },\n})\nvim.lsp.enable('gopls')\n```\n\nYou can find this snippet [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/compare/0e9d1f972a91acf5a0513319099ba41f7c09c30a...loichyan:mini.nvim:issue/complete-snippet).",
