            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is an intended behavior and the reason is described [in the comment above it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/301ee9f3afa2224b833de7c182574ba6c61e8c6e/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1234-L1236).\n\nThe presence of `S` label detail is *specifically* for this kind of situations:\n- If it is present, then the candidate will act as a snippet. Pressing any non-keyword character will lead to inserting a snippet and not to acting as that character.\n- If it is absent, the regular \"rules\" of completion accepting is applied.\n\nThe main idea behind this whole design is that user is only meant to select the entry and not have to specifically accept it. In both cases just typing whatever is meant to be typed (usually `<Space>`, or punctuation, or `<CR>`) does the job: if the candidate is not a snippet - characters will be inserted; if snippet - snippet session is started (as is required for snippet candidates).\n\nClosing as working as expected.",
