            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I just realized this is a crucial feature, as mini.completion accepts all non-keyword characters for confirming a completion. For LSP servers opt to return all items as snippets like gopls, removing this check would degrade the typing experience for other types of completion items, since mini.completion silently consumes the next character after you select an item. Anyway, I have found a [solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1938#issuecomment-3191585260) for my needs. Sorry for bothering!",
